# Defaults for running the workflows locally with nektos/act.
#
# Run one job at a time - `act` with no arguments starts every workflow at once,
# which means five ROS containers building in parallel:
#   act -W .github/workflows/ci.yml -j build-test-coverage
#   act -W .github/workflows/lint.yml
#
# Jobs that need the GitHub API (CodeQL, Scorecard, SBOM, release-please) skip
# themselves under act, and the SARIF and Codecov uploads are guarded the same
# way, so a local run finishes instead of retrying against an API that is not
# there.
#
# Secrets, when a job needs one:
#   act -s GITHUB_TOKEN="$(gh auth token)" -s CODECOV_TOKEN=... -s SONAR_TOKEN=...
# or put them in .secrets (KEY=value per line), which .gitignore already covers.
#
# ThreadSanitizer refuses to start when the kernel randomises more than 28
# address bits, which is the default on 6.x. Before running the tsan job:
#   sudo sysctl -w vm.mmap_rnd_bits=28
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
--container-architecture linux/amd64
